            <ArticleTitle>[Lifestyle changes for patients with coronary artery disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>357-8, 360-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Shortening the hospitalization period during an acute coronary syndrome can lead to a trivialization of the event, and especially causes many questions among patients about their future lifestyle. A secondary medical care in rehabilitation centers allows to combine the numerous benefits of physical training and to answer to their questioning, through to both a collective and individual therapeutic education.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
